CTA_FIRST = "Start with phase 1 →"

INTRO = [
    "A traditional VPN puts a remote user on the corporate network. Once the tunnel is up, the identity, device state and risk of that session barely matter: "
    "the user can reach whatever the network path allows. Attackers have spent years turning that design into an industry — VPN appliances on the internet are "
    "a favourite initial-access target, and a single successful auth often means lateral movement across whole subnets.",
    "Microsoft Entra Private Access is Microsoft's Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA) answer inside Global Secure Access. Users keep working from any network, "
    "but traffic to private apps is brokered per application (or per Quick Access segment) through outbound private network connectors, and Conditional Access "
    "decides whether that traffic is allowed. This guide builds that design with one non-negotiable rule: private-app traffic is granted only from devices "
    "that Intune marks compliant.",
]
NAMING = ("Scope: Microsoft Entra Private Access (the Private Access traffic forwarding profile under Global Secure Access) for Windows devices that are "
          "Microsoft Entra joined or hybrid joined and managed by Intune. Microsoft Entra Internet Access and the Microsoft traffic profile are mentioned only "
          "where they interact with this design. Tenant Recipes is not affiliated with Microsoft. Nothing on this page has been lab-tested by us; it is verified "
          "against Microsoft Learn documentation.")


